Along this characteristic line, we define
\[w(t) = \partial_x u(t,x(t), y_0).\]
Clearly, $w(0)=m_0$.

\textbf{Step 2: Deriving the evolution equation for the derivative along the characteristics}

We commence by rewriting the first equation of  system \eqref{eq:3} in the form:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:84}
