ref_dict.th:3sethomo:
\begin{theorem}\label{th:3sethomo}
Let $\Ga=(V,E)$ be a finite $3$-set-homogeneous graph. Then, up to complement, $\Ga$ is isomorphic either to one of the graphs: $\C_5$, $\K_n$, $\K_{m[b]}$, $\K_n\square\K_n$, or to one of the following graphs:
\begin{itemize}
\item[{\rm(1)}] the affine polar graph $\mathrm{VO}_{2m}^{\epsilon}(2)$ with $m\geq 1$ and $\epsilon \in \{+,-\}$;

\item[{\rm(2)}]  the elliptic orthogonal graph $\mathrm{\Gamma}(\mathrm{O}^-_6(q))$ with $q$ a prime power;

\item[{\rm(3)}] an orbital graph of the Higman-Sims group $\mathrm{HS}$ acting on $100$ points;

\item[{\rm(4)}] an orbital graph of the McLaughlin group $\mathrm{McL}$ acting on $275$ points.
\end{itemize}
In particular, all $3$-set-homogeneous graphs are $3$-homogeneous.
\end{theorem}

